RES osdtriplet
! ---- Constraint commands work inside AUT loop ----
! Run a short optimisation: CCY S2 + THC S3 as variables, TAS as constraint.
! LCON lists constraints after the loop; DCON ALL clears them.
AUT
CCY S2 0
THC S3 0
TAS = 0.01
TCO = 0.005
GO
LCON
DCON ALL
LCON
! ---- IMP sets improvement goal (silent state setter) ----
IMP 0.001
! ---- AUTOFUNC reports current autofunc (none defined) ----
AUTOFUNC
! ---- COST and WEIGHT: need CAPFN context ----
FOB 0
CAPFN
COST 1 6
WEIGHT 1 6
! ---- PRICE ALL: no data in this lens ----
PRICE ALL
! ---- DEFORM: no deformable surfaces in osdtriplet ----
DEFORM
! ---- AUTO (file save/reload) ≠ AUT (optimizer) ----
AUTO SAVE
AUTO RELOAD
! ---- INCR A 5: silently increments register A ----
INCR A 5
! ---- XXF P: Newtonian equation, find missing value (two given) ----
XXF P -50 25
! ---- XXFF P: Newtonian equation with 4 terms (find one) ----
XXFF P -50 25 30
! ---- OIF P: object-image-focal calculation ----
OIF P -200 50
! ---- DO: repeat FIR 3 times (deterministic) ----
DO FIR 1 3

! ---- AUT with no variables: must not crash ----
! Regression: AUT;GO without any variable used to ERROR STOP inside the slsqp
! initialization (killing the whole program).  Now it prints a clear message
! and returns.  Both the bare form and the with-constraint form are covered.
RES osdtriplet
AUT
GO
AUT
EFL = 50
GO
DCON ALL

! ---- Unified merit entries: operand vs constraint roles ----
! NAME target [weight] (no operator) adds an OBJECTIVE term, minimized as
! weight*(value-target)**2; NAME = value adds a hard constraint.  LCON lists
! both with their role.  The merit block round-trips through SAV/RES
! (including the weight), and DCON ALL clears operands too (historically
! operands survived and leaked across lens loads).
RES osdtriplet
TAR
SPO 0.0 2.0
EFL 55 0.5
TAS = 0.01
GO
LCON
SAV merittest
RES merittest
LCON
DCON ALL
LCON
